     * Refuse -- once -- if a previous submission of this exact change is
     * unaccounted for. `prior_outstanding` is whether the store's atomic
     * read-and-drop returned a record. Call before the prepare and the
     * biometric, so a refusal never costs the user a user verification.
     *
     * # Errors
     * `AmbiguousResubmit` when a previous submission was outstanding;
     * `OutOfOrder` if called more than once.
     */
    func admit(priorOutstanding: Bool) throws 
    
    /**
     * Declare that the write-ahead record is about to reach storage, which must
     * happen before anything can be broadcast. The record's contents are the
     * app's; this call is what makes skipping it an error rather than a silent
     * gap.
     *
     * # Errors
     * `OutOfOrder` if the attempt was never admitted, or is already armed.
     */
    func arm() throws 
    
    /**
     * The durable record key the app reads and writes under.
     */
    func key()  -> String
    
    /**
     * What to do with the record now the submission has finished. `answered`
     * is true only when the network said what it did with the transaction -- a
     * call that threw answered nothing.
     *
     * # Errors
     * `OutOfOrder` if the attempt was never armed, or is already settled.
     */
    func settle(answered: Bool) throws  -> SubmitRecordAction
    
}
