// Note that we don't yet support `indirect` for enums.
// See https://github.com/mozilla/uniffi-rs/issues/396 for further discussion.
/**
 * What the client should DO about a refused invite. The mapping from the
 * specific failure to one of these lives in the shared core, so native and web
 * cannot drift into showing the owner different things.
 */

public enum InviteRefusalFfi {
    
    /**
     * Nothing on this device could read the message, so it proves nothing
     * about who sent it. Drop it without a trace -- surfacing unreadable mail
     * would let any stranger who can reach the relay put rows on the owner's
     * screen.
     */
    case unreadable
    /**
     * It opened, so it genuinely came from a paired agent, but it failed a
     * binding check. Show it as refused; an owner debugging a misbehaving
     * agent must not be met with silence.
     */
    case notAuthentic
    /**
     * Authentic but outside the freshness window. Show it as expired.
     */
    case expired
    /**
     * Authentic, in date, and asking for something no owner may act on: a
     * signed lifetime outside the bounds a money decision may stand for.
     *
     * Distinct from [`Self::Expired`] because the recoveries are opposites.
     * An expired request is fixed by asking the agent to send a new one; this
     * one is reproduced exactly by resending it, so offering that retry loops
     * the owner.
     */
    case unreasonable
}


